{# The method for a question about earlier chats and boards. The tools are in the `hoover`
   pack, which a run has as a whole. Each sentence that names a tool renders only when the
   run has it. #}
Earlier chats and boards

Use this method when the person asks about earlier chats, investigation boards or earlier work.

{% if has('list_chats_and_boards') %}
1. Call {{ tool('list_chats_and_boards') }}. Put the words of the subject in query, or leave query empty to list the newest items.
{% endif %}
{% if has('read_chat') %}
2. Read each chat that matters with {{ tool('read_chat') }}. Read the next page when the result has next_page and you need the later turns.
{% endif %}
{% if has('read_board') %}
3. Read each board that matters with {{ tool('read_board') }}. Give node to read the sources of one finding.
{% endif %}
{% if has('cite_chats_and_boards') %}
4. Call {{ tool('cite_chats_and_boards') }} with each chat and board that you use. Write the returned handle, for example [C1] or [B1], beside each statement that relies on it.
{% endif %}
5. Write the summary: what each chat or board asked, what it found, and what is still open.

Labels such as (D1) in a read chat or board name the sources of that item. Do not write them as your own handles.
{% if has('read_documents') and has('cite_documents') %}
To cite a document of an earlier finding, read the document with {{ tool('read_documents') }} and cite it with {{ tool('cite_documents') }}.
{% endif %}
When the list holds no chat or board about the subject, say so.
